   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "Wilson added a question the earlier practice had not asked: whether the government had come to power by constitutional means. The thread runs from the conditions he put to Huerta in August 1913, through the de facto recognition of Carranza in 1915, to the flat refusal to recognize Tinoco in Costa Rica in 1917, where the new test was stated as a rule for the region."
  },
  {
   "kind": "document",
   "volumeId": "frus1913",
   "documentId": "d1028",
