   "text": "Non-recognition against coups, and the retreat from it, 1962–1979",
   "level": 1
  },
  {
   "kind": "prose",
   "text": "Kennedy tried to make recognition a lever against military coups in Peru, Ecuador, the Dominican Republic and Honduras, asking for a dated return to elected government; by December 1963 the Department judged the lever exhausted. From 1964 the practice turned to avoiding the question: continuity of relations in Brazil and Bolivia, consultation so as not to recognize first, and an open proposal to adopt the Estrada doctrine, under which a government is dealt with because it exists and not because it is legitimate."
  },
